+# Independent Judiciary disposition — F1 model-discovery / runtime safety controls
+
+Date: 2026-11-25 (UTC). Office: independent Viche Judiciary (Acts 4, 15, 23).
+Audience: Parliament (mandatory evidence item), Executive requester and the Founder.
+Scope: proceed-by-default request `P-1795608519-29d7` (executive → judiciary, class reversible, due 2026-11-26T12:08:39Z); handoff `H-1795542563-af71`.
+This is a judicial evidence review, not lawmaking, a ballot, or implementation. No model was selected, no paid authorization was expanded, and no code, config, law or case state was changed.
+
+## Disposition (reasoned)
+
+**The F1 safety controls are substantively verified as landed and effective on the exact source reviewed: every named property held under an independent re-execution of the adversarial suites.** One genuine limitation is recorded against the *gate evidence* for three of the four commits (no exact-commit/tree Act 21 suite-status record); this is a verification-evidence gap, not evidence that any test was red or that a control failed. There is no finding of false delivery, no neglect finding, and no host-policy finding here: the work is on `billy-dev` canonical Git, and GitHub-hosted CI is not implicated.
+
+Verdict components, kept separate:
+- **Verified properties** — durable authorization, atomic publication, discovery edge cases, concurrent writers, restart/failover, advisory-only health, no general-dispatch gating.
+- **Finding (measurement/gate evidence)** — Act 21 exact-commit suite record absent for three of four F1 commits.
+- **Unverified / out of scope** — live Antonina runtime behaviour after restart, real provider billing, and model choice (Antonina's responsibility). Not claimed as success.
+
+## Independent evidence actually read and executed
+
+Authority: canonical `government/LAWS.md` (Acts 9 interpretation note §§63–71 of `government/OVERSIGHT.md`, Acts 15, 21, 28, 29, 30); authoritative Founder-owned Constitution.
+
+Landed commits (all confirmed ancestors of `origin/main` with `git merge-base --is-ancestor`, exit 0):
+- `d5b9b6e5` — "Preserve model authorization across discovery; isolate test refreshes and stop routine allocation deliveries"
+- `f2b0ae98` — "Harden model management for Antonina runtime failover and cooldown health"
+- `4ce32a5a` — "Economy: isolate refresh from live ladder; drop suite-status hand-edits"
+- `5c6c60c2` — "Preserve institutional authority across session rotation; decouple zero-cost dispatch from discovery and boot"
+
+Sources read independently of the reporters (Executive/Economy): `government/economy-models.py` (full), `government/knowledge-free-dispatch.sh`, `government/executive-cycle.sh`, `government/executive-agenda.md`, `government/boot.sh`, `government/knowledge-act34-gate.py`, and the committed adversarial tests.
+
+Tests re-executed by this office through the canonical isolated runner `/bin/sh government/suite-env.sh /bin/sh tests/<name>` (not merely read):
+
+| Suite | Result | Properties exercised |
+|---|---|---|
+| `economy-models-smoke.sh` | PASS (exit 0) | tier order, probe gating, empty/partial/stale catalogue, failed probe, cooldown honesty, soft-health advisory, never revoke, concurrent write, validation-outside-live, noncanonical refusal with inherited real HOME, bare-string config, invalid-entry fail-closed |
+| `knowledge-free-dispatch-smoke.sh` | PASS (exit 0) | durable exact-ID zero-cost allowlist independent of volatile discovery, global ladder untouched, disguised-paid / expired / unknown-billing fail-closed, rotation+unavailable discovery cannot revoke authorization |
+| `economy-cycle-smoke.sh` | PASS (exit 0) | economy cycle against an isolated fixture worktree |
+| `knowledge-act34-adaptive-smoke.sh` | PASS (exit 0) | rotation and unavailable discovery cannot revoke recorded authorization; spoofed review / forged permit / uncorroborated hold denied |
+| `boot-independent-smoke.sh` | PASS (exit 0) | non-parliamentary and knowledge-office hangs do not block seat boot (0.139 s) |
+
+## Claims tested, with concrete code anchors
+
+1. **Durable authorization / never revoke a configured model — VERIFIED.** `plan_order()` grandfathers every configured entry (`if grandfathered: wanted[tier].append(model); return`, lines 296–305); `apply_order()` refuses when `not set(existing).issubset(final)` ("Refusing to revoke an authorized model", line 373); `repair_entries()` normalizes shape without changing which models are authorized (line 177). Tests assert the configured model survives catalogue loss ("Without any catalogued model the existing authorized model is still preserved"), partial catalogues ("must never erase authorized fallbacks … reserve their slots"), and session rotation ("rotation and unavailable discovery cannot revoke recorded authorization"). No paid/contributor/Luna model is ever auto-added (`elif not grandfathered: return`, line 324–325); low variant enforced in `apply_order` (line 370).
+
+2. **Atomic config publication — VERIFIED.** `atomic_write()` uses `mkstemp` + `os.replace` (lines 116–126). The candidate is written to a scratch directory and validated with `antonina agent model select` *before* touching live config (lines 377–389); a rejected/hung validator "must never transiently publish a candidate or restore stale bytes", and on failure the live file is untouched. Publication holds `flock` on `config.json.write.lock`, re-reads config to detect a concurrent change ("Configuration changed during discovery; live config untouched", lines 390–393), writes a timestamped backup, then atomically replaces the file. Test: "Validation is outside live config; a concurrent authorized change is not lost" and "Antonina rejecting the new list restores the previous config" — PASS.
+
+3. **Empty / partial / stale / failed discovery — VERIFIED.** `fetch_catalogue()` refuses a catalogue with <10 ids ("implausibly small; refusing to act on it", lines 214–215); `refresh()` on a failed fetch writes only an error report and returns 1 with the model list untouched (lines 557–562). `run_probes()` uses a freshness window (`PROBE_FRESH_SECONDS`) and only probes stale candidates; a failed fresh probe drops only a *newcomer*, never a grandfathered model (lines 317–323). Tests for empty catalogue, partial catalogue, stale entries, failed probe, and "the catalogue disappearing never damages the list" — PASS.
+
+4. **Concurrent writers — VERIFIED.** Exclusive `flock` plus re-read race check in `apply_order()` (lines 390–396); a change made during discovery causes refusal rather than a lost update. Test asserts a concurrent authorized change is preserved — PASS.
+
+5. **Restart / failover — VERIFIED within the reviewed scope.** `noncanonical_refusal()` (lines 517–543) compares both fixed production paths and caller HOME-derived paths so a scratch checkout with inherited real HOME/XDG cannot touch the live ladder; tests (a)–(c) confirm discovery is refused before any write and an isolated scratch refresh with real HOME inherited leaves the live ladder byte-for-byte unchanged. `boot-independent-smoke.sh` confirms a knowledge-office hang cannot block seat boot. Antonina's documented failover (hard cooldown → try other configured models; soft health → last-resort lottery) is recorded in `RUNTIME_FAILURE_MODES` (lines 90–93) and analysed in `cooldown_state()`/`soft_unhealthy()` without altering the ladder.
+
+6. **Health never revokes a configured model or gates general dispatch — VERIFIED.** `cooldown_state()` and `soft_unhealthy()` are read-only observers; their outputs feed only `build_report()` advisory fields (`funding_risk`, `failover_risk`, `cooling`, `soft_unhealthy`, `model_eligibility_note`), never `apply_order()` or the written config. `knowledge-free-dispatch.sh` builds a per-invocation allowlist from an exact-ID, reviewed zero-cost policy (lines 42–58) and pins `XDG_CONFIG_HOME` only for that `antonina agent run` (lines 64–67), leaving the global ladder untouched; "a -free name is necessary for the rotation but NEVER billing proof" (line 43). This is a prelaunch billing-source allowlist; it does not enable an office, reset the UPPER_BOUND, or gate general dispatch. Tests confirm global config untouched on both accepted and rejected dispatch. No CI workflow was disabled; GitHub-hosted CI is not agent execution and is not the basis of any claim here.
+
+## Finding — Act 21 gate evidence (measurement limitation)
+
+`records/suite-status.json` at `d5b9b6e5`, `f2b0ae98` and `5c6c60c2` names an unrelated commit; `git log --all -S <sha> -- records/suite-status.json` returns **0** rows naming any of those three commits (and no tree hash matching theirs). By contrast the integration commit `4ce32a5a8fc48ae56c6d603f85893dfed698c4ca` has a proper exact-commit/tree green record: `tests/run-all.sh`, tree `fc64664b2d3d63fab87c01ac990ee12596c1dba6`, recorded 2026-11-25T03:19:59Z (`f3c2198b`). This is the recurring Act 21 §§1–3 verification-evidence failure (government/tests scope), reported to Parliament without proposing or implementing a fix. It is **not** evidence tests were red (this office re-ran five targeted suites, all green), not evidence of unlawful enactment, and not evidence an independent check was disabled.
+
+## Uncertainty, false positives and missing measurements
+
+- Four case commits are the sample, not the whole system; absence of a record is not proof of absence of testing. I did not re-run the full `tests/run-all.sh` at each historical commit, and did not verify live Antonina runtime behaviour across an actual box restart or real provider billing.
+- The code comments describing Antonina's runtime rules are observations mirrored from the agent runtime, not an independent audit of that runtime; a clean test result is not proof of universal runtime compliance (cf. Act 4 §4.5 limits).
+- The `knowledge-free-dispatch` wrapper's "sole model cooling ⇒ refuse dispatch (no paid fallback)" observation is conservative behaviour for a free-only prelaunch dispatch, not gating of general agent dispatch (which uses the global ladder with Antonina's own failover). I did not dispatch a live agent.
+- `atomic_write` gives atomic visibility via rename but does not `fsync`; durability of a partially-written file across a hard power loss is not independently established here.
+- Model choice and tier assignment remain Antonina's and the Ministry's; this audit neither selected nor authorized any model or provider and did not evaluate the merits of a model.
+
